    "gitCommitMessage": "iOS discovery: one member at a time, scroll to pass\n\nApp Review read the swipe deck as another dating app. iOS now shows one\nmember filling the screen, moved through by scrolling; Android keeps the\ndeck untouched, and src/app/(app)/discover.tsx is the only file that\nchooses between them.\n\n- Photograph takes three quarters of the page and pages horizontally\n  through the member's pictures; tap left or right to move, because a\n  nested pager cannot be relied on to win the swipe.\n- Scrolling on records a pass, drawn live against the scroll as a colour\n  wash and a word so it is never silent. Gold for interest already sent,\n  red for a pass.\n- The bar under the photograph carries the two deliberate decisions,\n  express interest and save. It opens the full profile on a tap: dragging\n  up to open and scrolling up to move on were the same gesture, and\n  getting it wrong passed the person being read.\n- Revisiting someone passed is gated to Premium, corrected once on settle\n  rather than per frame, which was feeding itself into a scroll loop.\n- Every paid surface is sold on this screen: who is interested in you\n  (Gold), the interest allowance, going back, boosts, and the shortlist.\n\nAlso: guard the Meta SDK behind an Expo Go check so it stops red-boxing\nthe whole app at startup, and restore the route to Explore and events,\nwhich iOS had lost when the old Discover header was replaced.",
